# XSH pthread_attr_getdetachstate(), pthread_attr_setdetachstate()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# That the ID of a detached thread may not be joined or detached is an
# error with undefined behaviour (XSH 2.9.2), so it is not tested.

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getdetachstate.001
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getdetachstate.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getdetachstate.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       In a newly initialized attributes object,
           pthread_attr_getdetachstate() returns 0 and stores
           PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE.
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getdetachstate.002
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getdetachstate.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getdetachstate.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       pthread_attr_setdetachstate() with PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED,
           PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE and PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED again
           each returns 0, and pthread_attr_getdetachstate() then
           returns 0 and stores the value set.
test       t/002-round-trip.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getdetachstate.003
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getdetachstate.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2008
says       pthread_attr_setdetachstate() with a value that is neither
           PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED nor PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE returns
           EINVAL.
test       t/003-invalid.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_attr_getdetachstate.004
anchor     functions/pthread_attr_getdetachstate.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       A thread created with attributes set to
           PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE can be joined (pthread_join() returns
           0 and gives the routine's return value); a thread created with
           attributes set to PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED is created (0) and
           runs its routine once.
note       pthread_create() failing with EAGAIN is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/004-create.c
